that=E2=80=9D, you want {do=E2=80=99i}.
    If you fill in more sumti than a selbri has places for, the last sumt=
i have implied {do=E2=80=99e} sumtcita in front of them.



Furthermore, there is a word, {zi=E2=80=99o}, that you can fill a sumti p=
lace with to delete it from any selbri. {lo melbi be zi=E2=80=99o}, for i=
nstance, is just =E2=80=9CSomething beautiful=E2=80=9D, and does not incl=
ude the usual x2 of melbi, which is the observer who judges something to =
be beautiful. Thus, it can mean something like =E2=80=9CObjectively beaut=
iful.=E2=80=9D It does not state that nothing fills the sumti place which=
