re children=E2=80=9D
su=E2=80=99o remna na ku cu verba =E2=80=9CFor at least one human it=E2=80=
=99s not true that: It=E2=80=99s a child=E2=80=9D. See that the na ku is =
placed before cu, since a sumti can go only there. Had I only used na, it=
 would have to go after cu.

The quantifier is inverted, ro is turned into su=E2=80=99o. This is, of c=
ourse, only if the meaning of the bridi has to be preserved. This means t=
hat when the na ku is placed at the end of the bridi, only the selbri is =
negated but all the sumti and sumtcita are preserved, as can be seen by t=
hese three identical bridi:
